{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1d2-62fd-7091-a15f-687f76c867f4"},"sequence":61,"recorded_at":1780531400000117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"153c1ba2-b7e2-48bc-afc0-57c06fe1e8cb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"153c1ba2-b7e2-48bc-afc0-57c06fe1e8cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"153c1ba2-b7e2-48bc-afc0-57c06fe1e8cb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1d2-8aab-7462-866e-5658f733bf33"},"task_id":"01a0b1d2-8aab-7462-866e-5658f733bf33","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1d2-8aab-7462-866e-5658f733bf33","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-24z2b3/TASK-260830-24z2b3_rework-rev5.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES EVERY EARLIER PRECONDITION ON TASK-260830-24z2b3, including TASK-260830-24z2b3_rework-rev4.md. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-24z2b3 (implement-clone-bundle-and-canonical-session-types, first leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q). Change Request revision 4 was reviewed by RUN-260917-ab25c8 (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED with NO P1: one P2 and four small P3 items. Read TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-verdict-rev4.md and TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-evidence-rev4.tar.gz first. The reviewer grades P1-c, P2-alpha, P2-beta, P2-gamma and every P3 of the previous round as fixed, each with the reported vector plus vectors one step away, and every rev3 survivor re-planted on this tree and watched dying twice. None of that is in scope. The scope is one admit-hole and four hygiene items; this should be a short run.\n3|P2-delta — Build entries rewrite invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD and seal it, and two entries launder a native key past your own sanitizer. Section 1.6 says text MUST be valid UTF-8 and decoders MUST reject lone surrogate code points before canonicalization; the whole previous round rested on \"MUST NOT round a value and continue\". A Go string carrying `\\xff`, or the WTF-8 lone-surrogate bytes `\\xed\\xa0\\x80`, is not valid text — but every Build entry hands it to `json.Marshal`, which substitutes U+FFFD and continues, and the omit-self identity is then sealed over the REWRITTEN bytes. Witnessed through your production entries: `BuildCaptureManifest` admits `source_identity.native_session_id = \"native\\xff\"` and seals `\"native�\"`, and `DecodeCaptureManifest` admits the sealed bytes; the same for `opaque_identity`; a lone surrogate seals as three U+FFFD; and — the part that makes this a correctness hole rather than a cosmetic one — `\"native\\xff\"` and `\"native\\xfe\"` seal BYTE-IDENTICAL manifests, so two distinct inputs collapse to one identity. `IdentityDigest(\"op\\xff\")` equals `IdentityDigest(\"op�\")`. The same rewrite happens at `BuildCanonicalSession` (title, actor name, actor model, extension strings), `BuildCanonicalEvent` (evidence native_type, reason codes), the capture item `exclusion_reason`, the boundary `source_generation` (`ParseGeneration(\"g\\xff\")` admits) and identity/item extension strings. Meanwhile every OTHER native-key admission refuses that byte with `native key is not valid UTF-8` — the arm your own rev4 corpus added and TRACEABILITY.md states as the sanitizer's bound, so these two entries launder a value past a gate the package documents as closed. Fix: a shared valid-UTF-8 text gate at EVERY Build-side string admission; sanitize `NativeSessionID` and `OpaqueIdentity` before `EncodeNativeIdentity` marshals them (or validate them inside the exported entry). Negatives at `BuildCaptureManifest` (source identity native and opaque), at `IdentityDigest` (opaque) and one per Build shape, each asserting that NO U+FFFD appears in the sealed bytes — assert the sealed bytes, not merely that the call refused. Ship one narrowing mutant and its harness row. Note the shape for your own checking: this is the same \"re