{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c51d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1d2-62fd-7091-a15f-687f76c867f4"},"sequence":233,"recorded_at":1780531400000461,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"153c1ba2-b7e2-48bc-afc0-57c06fe1e8cb","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"153c1ba2-b7e2-48bc-afc0-57c06fe1e8cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"153c1ba2-b7e2-48bc-afc0-57c06fe1e8cb"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1d3d369770eb41b53d4cbec2558","text":"Read text file `/tmp/rev4r/task/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-24z2b3/TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-verdict-rev4.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 4\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260917-ab25c8 (claude-opus-5, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-24z2b3-4` revision 4, base\n5|`2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91`, candidate tree\n6|`33b52bcbe16b7dc2b40f8e54168768d2cc73f768` (23 paths; patch sha256\n7|`6bed41e87cfa6e9395bd725bdc840c1ad7ddac118aa783c5ef6065d3d2402b84`, verified).\n8|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (lines 10331–10546), §7.8,\n9|§10.2 and the common logical data model §1.6 (lines 244–337); the pinned\n10|sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0 as the producer states.\n11|\n12|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n13|\n14|The rev3 rework is real and complete on its own terms: P1-c, P2-α, P2-β, P2-γ\n15|and every P3 item of RUN-260917-62d051 is fixed, each graded below with my own\n16|executed evidence (the reported vector plus vectors one step away; every rev3\n17|survivor re-planted on this tree and watched die twice). What blocks acceptance\n18|is one new admit-hole of the same \"rewrite and continue\" class that P1-b and\n19|P1-c closed for numbers, found one §1.6 rule away at text:\n20|\n21|- **P2-δ** — every Build entry seals Go string inputs that are not valid UTF-8\n22|  after `encoding/json` has silently rewritten the bytes to U+FFFD, and for two\n23|  production entries (`BuildCaptureManifest`, `IdentityDigest`) this launders a\n24|  NativeIdentity native key past the sanitizer's own `native key is not valid\n25|  UTF-8` refusal — the arm the rev4 corpus added and TRACEABILITY.md states as\n26|  the sanitizer's bound. Two distinct inputs seal byte-identical objects.\n27|\n28|Nothing here is a Stop-The-Line. The rework scope is narrow (see the end).\n29|\n30|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree (`git archive\n31|33b52bcb…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-24z2b3/review-rev4/{candidate,pristine,probe}`,\n32|`.task-board` artifact dropped; the live worktree's temp-index tree OID was\n33|confirmed equal to `33b52bcb…` before anything ran). The live Story worktree,\n34|index, branch and HEAD were never touched (`git status` before and after:\n35|` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`, `?? internal/clonebundle/`). Every probe and\n36|plant ran through the production entry points; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` for\n37|every harness, no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` written; the candidate copy diffed clean\n38|against the pristine copy after every battery. Raw evidence is in\n39|`TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-evidence-rev4.tar.gz` (`logs/`, `logs/mutants/` one\n40|raw `go test` log per plant per run with the subprocess exit code,\n41|`logs/mutants-producer/run{1,2}/` the shipped harness's per-plant logs,\n42|`reviewer_mutants_rev4.py`, `site_plants.py`, `zz_rev4_probe*_test.go.txt`,\n43|`logs/probes-rev4*.log`, `logs/probes-rev3-on-rev4.log`).\n44|\n45|## 0. Rework verification — every rev3 finding graded\n46|\n47|| rev3 finding | Grade | Executed evidence (this run, new tree) |\n48||---|---|---|\n49|| P1-c non-message payloads escape the number model and the duplicate rule | **fixed** | `logs/probes-rev4.log` section A: all 24 non-message kinds × 8 vectors (`2^53+1`, `2^53`, `-(2^53)`, `2^60`, `1.5`, `1e2`, nested duplicate, array-nested duplicate) × 3 entries (Build, Decode unsealed, Decode resealed with the literal preserved textually) = 576 probes, **0 admitted**. Section B one step away: block-extension `2^53+1` under a non-message kind refused (B1); deep-array `2^53+1` refused (B2); `1.0`, `0.0`, `1E2`, `1e+2`, `1e-2`, `-1.5` refused as value faults; `1.`, `.5`, `01`, `+1`, `0x10`, `Infinity`, `NaN` refused at the frame (B4–B8); beyond-int64 refused (B7); safe edges seal exactly (`{\"n\":9007199254740991}` / `-9007199254740991`, B1b nested); `-0` seals as `0` (JCS form, stated bound). Sealed-bytes exactness asserted by the committed `TestCanonicalEventPayloadValueModel/build_sealed_exact` and `decode` rows. The rev3 probe battery (`zz_rev3_probe_test.go`) re-executed on this tree: all 28 N1 and 7 N2 vectors REFUSED (`logs/probes-rev3-on-rev4.log`). Producer `N-payload-number` KILLED 2/2. |\n50|| P2-α extension-value gate measured at 2 of 17 sites | **fixed** | 17 `checkExtensionsClosed` admission sites counted by grep (boundary.go:90/116/295/392/429, captureitem.go:143, capturebuild.go:308, event.go:298/559/607/751, identity.go:112/237, session.go:94/454, rawmanifest.go:319/483); `TestExtensionValueModelAtEverySite` has 17 rows mapping one-to-one. Class narrowing (drop the value model at exactly one site, whole suite as killer, `site_plants.py`): **17/17 KILLED 2/2** (`logs/mutants-ext-sites-runs1-2.log`, rev3: 2/17). Producer's 17 literal-keyed `N-ext-values-*` rows KILLED 2/2. |\n51|| P2-β `decodeRawEntries` equal-key duplicate at Decode unmeasured | **fixed** | `R3-raw-entries-dup-decode` (`key <= previous` → `<` at the Decode site, whole suite) KILLED 2/2 (rev3: SURVIVED 2/2); producer `N-raw-order-decode` KILLED 2/2; `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode/duplicate_entries` exists. |\n52|| P2-γ duplicate plan keys defeat one-per-plan-candidate | **fixed** | P5c `plan=[a,a,token] items=[a,b,token]` REFUSED \"plan keys carry duplicate\" (D1); one step away: `[a,token,token]` (D2), `[a,b,b]` (D3) REFUSED; extra/missing candidate REFUSED (D5/D6); `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` with `[a,a,token]` REFUSED (D7); `deriveRawComplete([a,a,token])=false` (D13); `N-plan-keys-dup` KILLED 2/2. |\n53|| P3-a′ content `null` passes the XOR | **fixed** | E1 `content:null`, E2 `descriptor:null`, E3 both null, E6 neither, E7 both REFUSED \"not exclusive\"; `N-block-content-null` KILLED 2/2. (E4 `content:null` beside a descriptor admits — the null is the absent arm; fine.) |\n54|| P3-b′ three misreporting details | **fixed** | G1 capture item / G2 actor / G3 content block extension `1.5` at decode now report \"carry a number outside the AX safe-integer model\"; bad key still reports \"reverse-DNS\" (G4). |\n55|| P3-c′ five unmeasured arms | **fixed** | Re-planted on this tree, all KILLED 2/2: `R3-proof-input-blocked`, `R3-ax-number-negative-edge`, `R3-sanitizer-zp`, `R3-payload-strict-object`, `R3-decode-external-null-parent` (rev3: SURVIVED 2/2 each). Producer rows `N-proof-input-blocked`, `N-ax-number-negative-edge`, `N-sanitizer-zp`, `N-payload-top-dup`, `N-decode-external-null-parent` KILLED 2/2. |\n56|| P3-d′ `EncodeNativeIdentity` rounds | **fixed** | F1 `2^60`, F2 `1.5`, F3 bad key, F5 nested duplicate REFUSED at encode; F4 safe max admits; P2u re-probed REFUSED; `N-encode-identity-extensions` KILLED 2/2. (The pre-validated-identity contract still holds for the identity fields themselves — F6 — which is where P2-δ lives.) |\n57|| P3-e′ `N-main-count` note | **fixed** | Split into `N-main-count-build` / `N-main-count-decode`, each KILLED 2/2; my `R3-decode-main-count` (decode site only, whole suite) KILLED 2/2. |\n58|| P3-f′ dead code | **fixed** | `sourceBasisObject`, `digestOrEmpty`, `digestOrEmptyDigest` gone (grep: none). |\n59|| P3-g′ refusal census | **fixed as disposed** | Version `1.0.1` at capture/session/event decode, `items`/`actors`/`raw_refs` not-an-array, schema of another type all REFUSED (H1–H8); coverprofile-driven census now 369 sites / 213 covered / 156 uncovered (rev3: 366/181/185, `logs/refusal-census.log`); the remainder is owner-grammar repeats (\"is not a digest/UUIDv7/timestamp/uint53\"), frame/unknown/missing-member arms per shape and infrastructure errors, stated as defense-in-depth in TRACEABILITY.md. |\n60|\n61|## Findings\n62|\n63|### P2-δ — Build entries rewrite invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD and seal it; two entries launder a native key past the sanitizer (`identity.go` `EncodeNativeIdentity`, `capturebuild.go:118-124`, `rawmanifest.go:431-443`, every Build string admission)\n64|\n65|§1.6: \"text MUST be valid UTF-8\"; \"Decoders MUST reject lone surrogate code\n66|points before canonicalization\"; and the whole rev3/rev4 round rests on \"MUST\n67|NOT round a value and continue\". A Go string carrying `\\xff` (or the WTF-8\n68|lone-surrogate bytes `\\xed\\xa0\\x80`) is not valid text; every Build entry\n69|passes it to `json.Marshal`, which substitutes U+FFFD and continues, and the\n70|omit-self identity is sealed over the rewritten bytes. Witnessed through the\n71|production entries (`logs/probes-rev4.log` section C, `logs/probes-rev4-k.log`):\n72|\n73|| Entry / member | Input | Result |\n74||---|---|---|\n75|| `BuildCaptureManifest` `source_identity.native_session_id` | `\"native\\xff\"` | **ADMITTED**, sealed `\"native�\"`, `DecodeCaptureManifest` of the sealed bytes admits (K1/K1b) |\n76|| `BuildCaptureManifest` `source_identity.opaque_identity` | `\"op\\xff\"` | **ADMITTED**, sealed `\"op�\"` (K2) |\n77|| `BuildCaptureManifest` `source_identity.native_session_id` | `\"native\\xed\\xa0\\x80\"` (lone surrogate) | **ADMITTED**, sealed `\"native���\"` (K3) |\n78|| `BuildCaptureManifest` | `\"native\\xff\"` vs `\"native\\xfe\"` | two distinct inputs seal **byte-identical** manifests (K4) |\n79|| `IdentityDigest` `opaque_identity` | `\"op\\xff\"` | **ADMITTED**; digest equals `IdentityDigest(\"op�\")` (K13/K14) |\n80|| `BuildCanonicalSession` title / actor name / actor model / extension string | `…\\xff` | ADMITTED, sealed with U+FFFD (C1–C4); lone-surrogate title sealed as three U+FFFD (C14) |\n81|| `BuildCanonicalEvent` evidence `native_type` / reason code | `…\\xff` | ADMITTED, sealed with U+FFFD (C6, C7) |\n82|| `BuildCaptureManifest` item `exclusion_reason` / boundary `source_generation` / item extension string / identity extension string | `…\\xff` | ADMITTED, sealed with U+FFFD (C9–C12); `ParseGeneration(\"g\\xff\")` admits (C16) |\n83|\n84|Every other native-key Build admission refuses the same byte (`native key is\n85|not valid UTF-8`): raw manifest `source_native_session_id` and entry keys (K5,\n86|K6), evidence `native_session_id`/`native_event_id` (K7, K8), actor\n87|`source_native_id` (K9), `external_source_ref` (K10), capture item keys (K11),\n88|`IdentityDigest` `native_session_id` (K12), and every Decode entry refuses the\n89|bytes at the frame (`environ.DecodeStrictObject`, C8). The hole is exactly the\n90|`EncodeNativeIdentity` path: `buildCaptureManifest` encodes the caller's\n91|`NativeIdentity` first and sanitizes only the re-decoded (already rewritten)\n92|bytes, and `IdentityDigest` sanitizes `NativeSessionID` but not\n93|`OpaqueIdentity` before encoding — so the invalid-UTF-8 member of the\n94|sanitizer's class, pinned by `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` (`\"a\\xffb\"`) and\n95|stated in TRACEABILITY.md (\"refuses … invalid UTF-8\"), is admitted by two\n96|production entries because `json.Marshal` rewrites it before the gate runs.\n97|The sanitizer corpus drives the function, not these entries — the driven half\n98|is right, the entry path is not.\n99|\n100|This is the P1-b/P1-c mechanism at a different §1.6 rule: the fix for numbers\n101|validated the literal before the host could round it; text has no such gate at\n102|Build, and this repository already treats U+FFFD substitution as an admit hole\n103|(`internal/environ` refuses lone-surrogate escapes at Decode for exactly this\n104|reason). Graded P2 rather than P1: Decode refuses the bytes, the sealed output\n105|is well-formed, and the affected inputs are core-produced Go strings; but a\n106|production gate admits what it must reject and two different inputs collide on\n107|one identity.\n108|\n109|Fix: one shared text gate (`utf8.ValidString`, refusing invalid UTF-8) at every\n110|Build-side string admission — title, actor name/model, native_type, reason\n111|codes, exclusion_reason, generation, extension string values (walk the\n112|marshalled bytes or the Go values before `encodeExtensions` accepts them) — and\n113|sanitize `NativeSessionID`/`OpaqueIdentity` before `EncodeNativeIdentity`\n114|marshals them (or make the exported entry validate them the way it now\n115|validates extensions). Negatives at both laundering entries\n116|(`BuildCaptureManifest` source identity, `IdentityDigest` opaque identity) plus\n117|one per Build shape; assert the sealed bytes never carry U+FFFD for an input\n118|that did not; one narrowing mutant (admit exactly one invalid byte value, e.g.\n119|`\\xff`, or exempt exactly one member).\n120|\n121|### P3 — bounds, precision, hygiene\n122|\n123|- P3-a″ **Producer evidence archive is contaminated.**\n124|  `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (rev4) carries, beside the\n125|  27 command logs, package logs and the 2×65 per-plant logs it describes, 20+\n126|  foreign artifacts dated 2026-09-16/17 from the TASK-260909-2ez769 review\n127|  (`attacks.py`, `attacks.json`, `test_r4_cr_smuggle.py`, `test_r4_bypass_new.py`,\n128|  `test_r3_*_rerun.py`, `capture_cr.py`, `replay_mutants.py`,\n129|  `review-evidence-rev4.zip`, `review-logbook-rev4.md`, `mypy.log`, …) and a\n130|  `__pycache__/` with three `.pyc` files — the contract says no `__pycache__`,\n131|  and the MANIFEST.sha256 lists them as if they were this task's evidence.\n132|  Rebuild the archive from a task-scoped directory (the rev4 logs themselves\n133|  are fine: `mutants-run{1,2}.log` reproduce exactly in my runs).\n134|- P3-b″ **TRACEABILITY.md over-claims a bound**: \"`-0` and leading-`+`/leading-zero\n135|  integer literals in extension values and payloads admit\". Only `-0` admits\n136|  (sealed as `0`, the JCS form); `+1` and `01` are refused at the frame gate\n137|  (`decodeStrictObject`/`checkExtensionValues` cannot tokenize them — probes B8:\n138|  \"not a JSON object\"). Fix the sentence.\n139|- P3-c″ **Build-side reason-code duplicate unmeasured**: `R4-reason-codes-dup-build`\n140|  (`reason <= previousReason` → `<` in `buildSourceEvidence`) SURVIVED the whole\n141|  suite 2/2; the arm works (L1: `ReasonCodes: [\"a\",\"a\"]` at Build REFUSED \"not\n142|  sorted unique\") but the build rows have only `unsorted` (`b,a`) and `empty`;\n143|  the duplicate row exists at Decode only. Same class as P2-β one site over:\n144|  add the build duplicate row and a harness row.\n145|- P3-d″ **Producer ticked reviewer-owned checklist rows.** The live checklist\n146|  arrived with \"Implementation matches AC\", \"Solution fits project\n147|  architecture\", \"Tests green\", \"Gate … attacked, not read\" and \"If review does\n148|  not accept …\" all checked; those are verdict rows and are reset by this\n149|  review. When \"reset and re-complete the checklist\" is the brief, re-complete\n150|  the producer rows only.\n151|- Informational (not defects, no action required unless cheap): per-member\n152|  narrowings that survive because the class is pinned by one member —\n153|  `R4-sanitizer-c1-u009f` (stated owner-informational), `R4-sanitizer-c0-u0001`\n154|  (C0 pinned by U+0000/U+001F/U+007F), `R4-plan-dup-other-key`\n155|  (`store/token-cache` duplicate; the row duplicates `store/blob-a`),\n156|  `R4-cwd-dotdot` (bare `..`; row has `../escape`), `R4-unstable-reason-code`\n157|  (`source_quiescent`; row has `tired`), `R4-evidence-partial-operation`\n158|  (`partial`+operation; rows use `exact`) — every arm refuses when probed (L2–L6).\n159|  Spec-silent behaviours worth a stated line: an actor whose\n160|  `parent_actor_id` is itself or names no actor is admitted (I23/I24); plan\n161|  keys are matched as a set, so an unsorted permutation of the plan admits\n162|  (D4) while the §7.8 sink is sorted unique; content-block `content` is always\n163|  a string, so a `json` block carries its JSON as text (E9).\n164|\n165|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n166|\n167|1. **Spec fidelity, member level** — re-extracted every closed shape from the\n168|   pinned text and compared member-for-member: Raw Object Manifest (11\n169|   members) and `RawObjectEntry` (5; the prose \"and extensions\" is overridden\n170|   by the closed shape), Capture Manifest (17), Source Basis `ax_session` (6) /\n171|   `external_native` (3), `CaptureItem` (7, nine classes), Capture Boundary\n172|   `stable` (3) / `unstable_archive` (8), `StableSnapshotProof` (9, four\n173|   kinds), `NativeIdentity` (6, three kinds), `WorkspaceBinding` (8),\n174|   Canonical Session (14), `Actor` (7, three kinds), Canonical Event (14, 26\n175|   kinds, four visibilities), `SourceEvidence` (9, four statuses),\n176|   `RawReference` (4), eight content-block types; every bound\n177|   ([1..512]/[1..4096]/[1..1024]/[0..64]/[0..128]/[0..65536]/[1..1000000]/\n178|   [1..1024]/[0..9]/[1..128][0..128]/64 KiB) matches. The rev3→rev4 production\n179|   delta (`git diff d5b5b0ee…33b52bcb`) touches only `event.go` (payload value\n180|   model), `capturebuild.go` (plan-key duplicates), `captureitem.go`/`session.go`\n181|   (detail text), `identity.go` (encode validation), `decode.go` (one error\n182|   value), `boundary.go` (dead code removed); `blobref.go` and `rawmanifest.go`\n183|   are byte-identical to rev3, so the rev3 verification of descriptor linking,\n184|   exclusion and blob install stands and was re-executed here.\n185|2. **Row-21 exclusion** — `refuseExcludedMember` at all four\n186|   construction/decode paths; every handoff class plus `../escape` and\n187|   `state/../../escape` has a constructor negative in both manifests and a\n188|   decode negative; absolute paths are refused one gate earlier by the\n189|   sanitizer. The rev3 P3x rows re-executed unchanged (`host-channel\\trust.json`,\n190|   `HOST-CHANNEL/…`, `x/host-channel/…`, bare `lock` admit — the hosttrust\n191|   matcher's anchored STATE_DIR-relative contract, outside this leaf). Producer\n192|   `N-exclusion-config` KILLED 2/2.\n193|3. **provhost bound** — `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`\n194|   PASS on the exact tree (`logs/provhost-census.log`); module grep: non-test\n195|   `VerifyObjectIdentity` callers are only `internal/sessrepo` (5 sites);\n196|   `clonebundle` production calls `CalculateObjectIdentity` ×1 and\n197|   `Canonicalize` ×3 only; nothing imports `clonebundle`. Producer\n198|   `N-descriptor-claim-agreement`, `N-install-site-claim`, `N-descriptor-id-link`\n199|   KILLED 2/2; rev3 P1/P1x/P1y/P1z/P1w re-executed REFUSED.\n200|4. **Blob install** — unchanged code; rev3 P14 series re-executed on this tree:\n201|   short/long/same-length-wrong bytes REFUSED, `blob_id != chunk digest` REFUSED\n202|   at the claim, correct install ADMITTED, re-install different bytes REFUSED\n203|   (no-replace), same bytes ADMITTED, owner refuses size/chunk disagreement.\n204|   Durability bound stated and accurate (no write path in this package;\n205|   `internal/localstore` green in the four-package run).\n206|5. **Mutation** — shipped harness reproduced in the isolated copy: 64 KILLED +\n207|   `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED, twice, tree restored (`logs/mutants-producer-runs{1,2}.log`,\n208|   130 per-plant logs); rev3 survivors 7/7 KILLED 2/2; per-site class plants\n209|   17/17 KILLED 2/2; my rev4 plants (`reviewer_mutants_rev4.py`, 23 rows × 2):\n210|   the brief's four classes KILLED (`R4-unknown-ignores-one`,\n211|   `R4-excluded-set-missing-runtime_state`, `R4-raw-subset-admits-transient_lock`,\n212|   sorted-unique duplicates via `R3-raw-entries-dup-decode`/`R4-rawrefs-dup-build`,\n213|   sanitizer control via the producer's `N-sanitizer-control`), plus\n214|   `R4-heads-skip-last-{build,decode}`, `R4-sanitizer-schemeless-cred`,\n215|   `R4-drive-prefix-backslash`, `R4-inline-65537`, `R4-ordinal-edge`,\n216|   `R4-actor-external-null-parent-build`, `R4-digests-equal-one-order`,\n217|   `R4-unstable-operator-explicit` (re-planted after a compile-fail first\n218|   shape), `R4-generation-empty`, `R4-immutable-identity-required` KILLED 2/2;\n219|   `C4-comment-control` SURVIVED 2/2; the seven survivors are P3-c″ and the\n220|   informational per-member rows above.\n221|6. **Race gate** — see the next section.\n222|7. **Hygiene** — `gofmt -l` empty; `go vet` clean; `go build ./...` OK; `go test\n223|   ./internal/clonebundle ./internal/provhost ./internal/localstore\n224|   ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1` all ok (`logs/four-packages.log`);\n225|   `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` exit 0 (bindings=68,\n226|   clauses 49/569 — `internal/traceability` untouched); `cataloggen -adopted\n227|   -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree;\n228|   `git diff --check` clean; changed paths are exactly the 23 candidate paths\n229|   (README/LOGBOOK purely additive, +27/+10; nothing outside\n230|   `internal/clonebundle`; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR; the CR validation\n231|   log reports `required=27 green=27 failed=0 missing=0`). README section has\n232|   the three test commands and no capability claim. LOGBOOK entry newest-first.\n233|   Package coverage 86.8% statements. All 32 matrix-named tests exist; the\n234|   conformance matrix's 18-of-18 ratio and call sites check out. Sibling bounds\n235|   stated in doc.go, TRACEABILITY.md and results.md.\n236|\n237|## Race gate (item 7)\n238|\n239|`internal/sessquery` is untouched by this change (`go list -deps` and\n240|`-test -deps` of sessquery: 0 clonebundle; nothing imports clonebundle). The\n241|rev4 Change Request validation ran the 27-command suite with the landed\n242|`-timeout 25m` and is green (`ok internal/sessquery 390.722s` in the producer's